arguments.report:
## Root cause
`(*context).Scheme()` in /echo/context.go returned the raw `X-Forwarded-Proto` / `X-Forwarded-Protocol` / `X-Url-Scheme` header values verbatim whenever they were non-empty, with no validation. So a bogus value (e.g. `X-Forwarded-Proto: bogus`) was returned as the scheme instead of being ignored, and mixed-case values (`HTTP`) were returned un-normalized (violating the documented contract "Scheme returns the HTTP protocol scheme, `http` or `https`").

## Fix (only file changed by me: /echo/context.go)
Precedence kept exactly as before (TLS → X-Forwarded-Proto → X-Forwarded-Protocol → X-Forwarded-Ssl=="on" → X-Url-Scheme → "http"); only validation was added via a new helper. Lines 252–288 (Scheme at 252, helper at 277):

```go
 	if scheme := schemeFromHeader(c.request.Header.Get(HeaderXForwardedProto)); scheme != "" {
 		return scheme
 	}
 	if scheme := schemeFromHeader(c.request.Header.Get(HeaderXForwardedProtocol)); scheme != "" {
 		return scheme
 	}
 	if ssl := c.request.Header.Get(HeaderXForwardedSsl); ssl == "on" {
 		return "https"
 	}
 	if scheme := schemeFromHeader(c.request.Header.Get(HeaderXUrlScheme)); scheme != "" {
 		return scheme
 	}
 	return "http"
 }

// schemeFromHeader returns the normalized scheme (`http` or `https`) when the
// given header value is a valid scheme (case insensitive), otherwise it returns
// an empty string so the caller can ignore the invalid value and fall back to
// the next source of information.
func schemeFromHeader(value string) string {
 	if strings.EqualFold(value, "http") {
 		return "http"
 	}
 	if strings.EqualFold(value, "https") {
 		return "https"
 	}
 	return ""
 }
```
`git diff context.go` = 3 call sites changed (`Header.Get` wrapped in `schemeFromHeader`) + 14 new lines (helper). No other file touched by me. gofmt clean.

